"settings.music.appleMusicDetail2" = "Apple Music mode reads playback information from Music.app through the public AppleScript interface, which requires Automation permission. Demo data exists only for interface development, always carries a DEMO DATA badge, is never treated as real playback, and never substitutes for Apple Music when it is unavailable.";
"settings.music.interpolationNote" = "Playback position is not polled; it is interpolated locally — advancing while playing, frozen while paused, reset on track change, and corrected once per poll.";
"settings.spectrum.binningNote" = "Bands are distributed logarithmically, covering 20 Hz – 20 kHz. The hop is fixed at a quarter of the FFT size (75% overlap). Changing any of the above rebuilds the analyser.";
"settings.spectrum.smoothingNote" = "Sensitivity is overall gain: it shifts the scale without inventing frequency structure. Attack is fixed at the fast setting so drum transients are not softened; this controls the release.";
"settings.spectrum.frameRateNote" = "Measured: the DSP itself costs about 0.03 ms per run (roughly 0.2% CPU). The real cost is one interface update per publish, so the refresh rate directly determines CPU usage.";
"settings.clock.worldClockNote" = "Click the large time display in the HUD to cycle: TRACK → each city → TRACK. The order and enabled state are below. Time zones come from the system database; daylight saving is handled automatically.";
"settings.window.clickThroughNote" = "In this mode the panel stops receiving mouse events. Transport buttons will not respond; turn the mode off from the menu bar.";
"settings.window.resetNote" = "The first launch and “Reset Position” both place the panel at the top-right of the main display (the one with the menu bar), so it never lands on a virtual display or a disconnected external screen.";
"diagnostics.silentNote" = "PCM is arriving but every sample is zero — capture is working, the source is silent.";
